\/b> everyone's cooperation.","hungarian":"A projekt sikere mindenki egy\u00fcttm\u0171k\u00f6d\u00e9s\u00e9t\u0151l f\u00fcgg.","explanation":"<b>depend on<\/b> \u2014 f\u00fcgg valamit\u0151l. Fontos: \"depend ON\", nem \"depend from\"."},{"id":95,"category":"prepositions","english":"The success of the project depends <b>on<\/b> everyone's cooperation.","hungarian":"A projekt sikere mindenki egy\u00fcttm\u0171k\u00f6d\u00e9s\u00e9t\u0151l f\u00fcgg.","explanation":"<b>depend on<\/b> \u2014 f\u00fcgg valamit\u0151l. Fontos: \"depend ON\", nem \"depend from\"."},{"id":47,"category":"prepositions","english":"She's very good <b>at<\/b> solving complex problems.","hungarian":"Nagyon j\u00f3 \u00f6sszetett probl\u00e9m\u00e1k megold\u00e1s\u00e1ban.","explanation":"<b>good at<\/b> \u2014 j\u00f3 valamiben. Az \"at\" ut\u00e1n gerund (-ing) vagy f\u0151n\u00e9v j\u00f6n."},{"id":96,"category":"prepositions","english":"She's very good <b>at<\/b> solving complex problems.","hungarian":"Nagyon j\u00f3 \u00f6sszetett probl\u00e9m\u00e1k megold\u00e1s\u00e1ban.","explanation":"<b>good at<\/b> \u2014 j\u00f3 valamiben. Az \"at\" ut\u00e1n gerund (-ing) vagy f\u0151n\u00e9v j\u00f6n."},{"id":48,"category":"prepositions","english":"He's been interested <b>in<\/b> astronomy since childhood.","hungarian":"Gyerekkora \u00f3ta \u00e9rdekli a csillag\u00e1szat.","explanation":"<b>interested in<\/b> \u2014 \u00e9rdekli valami. Fontos: \"in\", nem \"for\" vagy \"about\"."},{"id":97,"category":"prepositions","english":"He's been interested <b>in<\/b> astronomy since childhood.","hungarian":"Gyerekkora \u00f3ta \u00e9rdekli a csillag\u00e1szat.","explanation":"<b>interested in<\/b> \u2014 \u00e9rdekli valami. Fontos: \"in\", nem \"for\" vagy \"about\"."},{"id":49,"category":"prepositions","english":"I'm really proud <b>of<\/b> what you've achieved.","hungarian":"Nagyon b\u00fcszke vagyok arra, amit el\u00e9rt\u00e9l.","explanation":"<b>proud of<\/b> \u2014 b\u00fcszke valamire. Angolul \"of\", nem \"from\" vagy \"about\"."},{"id":98,"category":"prepositions","english":"I'm really proud <b>of<\/b> what you've achieved.","hungarian":"Nagyon b\u00fcszke vagyok arra, amit el\u00e9rt\u00e9l.","explanation":"<b>proud of<\/b> \u2014 b\u00fcszke valamire. Angolul \"of\", nem \"from\" vagy \"about\"."},{"id":99,"category":"present_perfect_vs_past","english":"I <b>have seen<\/b> that film \u2014 it's brilliant.","hungarian":"L\u00e1ttam azt a filmet \u2014 zseni\u00e1lis.","explanation":"<b>Present perfect<\/b> \u2014 a tapasztalat relev\u00e1ns a jelenben, az id\u0151pont nem sz\u00e1m\u00edt. Nem mondan\u00e1nk \"I saw it yesterday\" ha az id\u0151pontot is meg akarjuk adni."},{"id":100,"category":"present_perfect_vs_past","english":"She <b>finished<\/b> the report an hour ago.","hungarian":"Egy \u00f3r\u00e1ja fejezte be a jelent\u00e9st.","explanation":"<b>Past simple<\/b> \u2014 konkr\u00e9t m\u00faltbeli id\u0151pont (ago, yesterday, last week). Ilyenkor NEM haszn\u00e1lunk present perfectet!"},{"id":101,"category":"present_perfect_vs_past","english":"Have you ever <b>been<\/b> to Japan?","hungarian":"Volt\u00e1l m\u00e1r valaha Jap\u00e1nban?","explanation":"<b>Present perfect + ever<\/b> \u2014 \u00e9letbeli tapasztalat k\u00e9rdez\u00e9se. Az \"ever\" mindig present perfecttel j\u00e1r k\u00e9rd\u00e9sben."},{"id":102,"category":"present_perfect_vs_past","english":"They <b>have just announced<\/b> the results.","hungarian":"Az im\u00e9nt hirdett\u00e9k ki az eredm\u00e9nyeket.","explanation":"<b>Present perfect + just<\/b> \u2014 p\u00e1r pillanata t\u00f6rt\u00e9nt, a hat\u00e1s m\u00e9g \u00e9rz\u0151dik. A \"just\" ilyenkor NEM past simple-lel j\u00e1r."},{"id":103,"category":"present_perfect_vs_past","english":"I <b>lost<\/b> my keys yesterday.","hungarian":"Tegnap elvesztettem a kulcsaimat.","explanation":"<b>Past simple<\/b> \u2014 \"yesterday\" konkr\u00e9t id\u0151pontot ad meg, ez\u00e9rt past simple sz\u00fcks\u00e9ges, nem present perfect."},{"id":104,"category":"gerund_vs_infinitive","english":"She enjoys <b>reading<\/b> historical novels.","hungarian":"Szereti olvasni a t\u00f6rt\u00e9nelmi reg\u00e9nyeket.","explanation":"<b>enjoy + gerund (-ing)<\/b> \u2014 az \"enjoy\" ut\u00e1n mindig -ing alak j\u00f6n, soha infinitive. Hasonl\u00f3an: avoid, finish, consider, mind, keep."},{"id":105,"category":"gerund_vs_infinitive","english":"He decided <b>to change<\/b> his career.","hungarian":"Elhat\u00e1rozta, hogy p\u00e1ly\u00e1t v\u00e1ltoztat.","explanation":"<b>decide + infinitive (to)<\/b> \u2014 a \"decide\" ut\u00e1n to + infinitive j\u00f6n. Hasonl\u00f3an: want, plan, hope, agree, refuse, manage."},{"id":106,"category":"gerund_vs_infinitive","english":"I remembered <b>to lock<\/b> the door before leaving.","hungarian":"Eml\u00e9keztem r\u00e1, hogy kulcsra z\u00e1rjam az ajt\u00f3t indul\u00e1s el\u0151tt.","explanation":"<b>remember + to infinitive<\/b> \u2014 nem felejtett el megtenni valamit (j\u00f6v\u0151re ir\u00e1nyul\u00f3). K\u00fcl\u00f6nb\u00f6zik ett\u0151l: \"I remember locking it\" = eml\u00e9kszem, hogy megtettem."},{"id":107,"category":"gerund_vs_infinitive","english":"They stopped <b>to have<\/b> lunch at noon.","hungarian":"Meg\u00e1lltak eb\u00e9delni d\u00e9lben.","explanation":"<b>stop + to infinitive<\/b> \u2014 meg\u00e1lltak az\u00e9rt, hogy tegyenek valamit. K\u00fcl\u00f6nb\u00f6zik: \"stopped smoking\" = abbahagyt\u00e1k a doh\u00e1nyz\u00e1st (gerund = a cselekv\u00e9st hagyj\u00e1k abba)."},{"id":108,"category":"articles","english":"She plays <b>the<\/b> piano beautifully.","hungarian":"Gy\u00f6ny\u00f6r\u0171en zongor\u00e1zik.","explanation":"<b>the + hangszer neve<\/b> \u2014 hangszerj\u00e1t\u00e9k el\u0151tt mindig \"the\" kell. \"She plays piano\" helytelen. \"She is a pianist\" viszont j\u00f3, mert foglalkoz\u00e1s."},{"id":109,"category":"articles","english":"He is <b>a<\/b> doctor at <b>the<\/b> local hospital.","hungarian":"Orvos a helyi k\u00f3rh\u00e1zban.","explanation":"<b>a doctor<\/b> \u2014 foglalkoz\u00e1s, nem meghat\u00e1rozott szem\u00e9ly \u2192 hat\u00e1rozatlan n\u00e9vel\u0151. <b>the hospital<\/b> \u2014 konkr\u00e9t, m\u00e1r ismert k\u00f3rh\u00e1z \u2192 hat\u00e1rozott n\u00e9vel\u0151."},{"id":110,"category":"articles","english":"I go to <b>work<\/b> by <b>bus<\/b>.","hungarian":"Busszal j\u00e1rok munk\u00e1ba.","explanation":"<b>go to work \/ by bus<\/b> \u2014 n\u00e9vel\u0151 n\u00e9lk\u00fcli kifejez\u00e9sek. \"Work\" \u00e9s k\u00f6zleked\u00e9si eszk\u00f6z\u00f6k \"by\" ut\u00e1n n\u00e9vel\u0151 n\u00e9lk\u00fcl \u00e1llnak."},{"id":111,"category":"articles","english":"<b>The<\/b> Amazon is <b>the<\/b> longest river in South America.","hungarian":"Az Amazonas D\u00e9l-Amerika leghosszabb foly\u00f3ja.","explanation":"<b>the<\/b> + foly\u00f3nevekhez, tengerekhez, hegyl\u00e1ncokhoz (the Alps, the Pacific). V\u00e1rosok, orsz\u00e1gok el\u0151tt \u00e1ltal\u00e1ban nincs n\u00e9vel\u0151."},{"id":112,"category":"verb_patterns","english":"Let me <b>help<\/b> you with that.","hungarian":"Hadd seg\u00edtsek abban.","explanation":"<b>let + object + bare infinitive<\/b> \u2014 a \"let\" ut\u00e1n t\u00e1rgy, majd n\u00e9vel\u0151 n\u00e9lk\u00fcli infinitive j\u00f6n. NEM \"let me to help\"."},{"id":113,"category":"verb_patterns","english":"She made him <b>apologize<\/b> publicly.","hungarian":"Nyilv\u00e1nosan bocs\u00e1natot k\u00e9rette vele.","explanation":"<b>make + object + bare infinitive<\/b> \u2014 k\u00e9nyszert fejez ki. Hasonl\u00f3an: \"have him do it\". Passz\u00edvban viszont: \"He was made to apologize.\""},{"id":114,"category":"verb_patterns","english":"I saw her <b>crossing<\/b> the street in a hurry.","hungarian":"L\u00e1ttam, ahogy siet \u00e1ts\u00e9t\u00e1lni az utc\u00e1n.","explanation":"<b>see + object + -ing<\/b> \u2014 r\u00e9szleges megfigyel\u00e9s, folyamat k\u00f6zben. \"I saw her cross the street\" = az eg\u00e9sz cselekv\u00e9st l\u00e1ttam elej\u00e9t\u0151l v\u00e9g\u00e9ig (bare infinitive)."}],"categories":["articles","conditional","could_have","false_friends","gerund_vs_infinitive","have_been","might_have","must_have","passive","phrasal_verbs","prepositions","present_perfect_vs_past","reported_speech","should_have","used_to","verb_patterns","wish_if_only","would_have"],"activeCategory":"all"},"url":"\/sentence-trainer","version":"8f4ca32974876a648b2aa33abd3f4aea","sharedProps":["errors","name","auth","sidebarOpen","flash"]}</script><div id="app"></div><?php /**PATH /Applications/XAMPP/xamppfiles/htdocs/topEwords/storage/framework/views/85d2f2bca6b256eec0ad8bc2c744acc2.blade.php ENDPATH**/ ?>